Customizing Cypress test runner behavior to capture screenshots:

In your Cypress test or integration file `cypress/integration/your_spec_file.js`, you can use the following code to enable screenshot capture and compare it dynamically:

```javascript
Cypress.Commands.add('spyAndTakeScreenshot', { prevSubject: 'any' }, async (subject) => {
  // Add screenshot and save it
  await Cypress.wait(100);
  await subject.screenshot({
    clip: subject, // include the entirety of the subject element
    path: 'spy-and-screenshot.png',
    // Dynamic filename to avoid overwriting the file on each run
    // Comment or delete if you want to overwrite the image each run
    fileName: `spy-and-screenshot-${Cypress.moment().format('YYYYMMDD_HH_mm_ss')}`,
  });

  // Compare with previous snapshot
  await Cypress.skipExistsThenAdd();
});
```

To capture a screenshot of an element or vue(i) framework component input/submit button, chain your `spyAndTakeScreenshot` custom command with the `cy.get(selector).trigger('submit')` commands. The custom command takes extra time to capture a screenshot dynamically and compare it to previous snapshots, so it should be used for performance-intensive or visual testing.

